{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":49,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Luke.5","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Luke","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Luke 5","reference":"Luke 5","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Matt. iv, 18; Mark i, 16.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":4,"text":"Their net brake - Began to tear.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":5,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":6,"text":"Depart from me, for I am a sinful man - And therefore not worthy to be in thy presence.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":7,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":8,"text":"They forsook all and followed him - They had followed him before, John i, 43, but not so as to forsake all.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":9,"text":"Till now, they wrought at their ordinary calling.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":10,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":11,"text":"Matt. viii, 2; Mark i, 40.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":12,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":13,"text":"Lev. xiv, 2.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":14,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":15,"text":"He withdrew - The expression in the original implies, that he did so frequently.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":16,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":17,"text":"Sitting by - As being more honourable than the bulk of the congregation, who stood.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":18,"text":"And the power of the Lord was present to heal them - To heal the sickness of their souls, as well as all bodily diseases.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":19,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":20,"text":"Matt. ix, 2; Mark ii, 3.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":21,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":22,"text":"Not being able to bring him in through the multitude, they went round about by a back passage, and going up the stairs on the outside, they came upon the flat-roofed house, and let him down through the trap door, such as was on the top of most of the Jewish houses: doubtless, with such circumspection as the circumstances plainly required.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":23,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":24,"text":"We have seen strange things today - Sins forgiven, miracles wrought.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":25,"text":"27.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":26,"text":"Matt. ix, 9; Mark ii, 14.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":27,"scriptureVerseEnd":27},{"verse":27,"text":"28.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":28,"text":"Leaving all - His business and gain.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":28,"scriptureVerseEnd":28},{"verse":29,"text":"29.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":30,"text":"And Levi made him a great entertainment - It was necessarily great, because of the great number of guests.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":29,"scriptureVerseEnd":29},{"verse":31,"text":"33.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":33,"scriptureVerseEnd":33},{"verse":32,"text":"Make prayers - Long and solemn.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":33,"scriptureVerseEnd":33},{"verse":33,"text":"Matt. ix, 14; Mark ii, 18.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":33,"scriptureVerseEnd":33},{"verse":34,"text":"34.","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":34,"scriptureVerseEnd":34},{"verse":35,"text":"Can ye make - That is, is it proper to make men fast and mourn, during a festival solemnity?","sourceParagraph":16,"scriptureVerseStart":34,"scriptureVerseEnd":34},{"verse":36,"text":"36.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":36,"scriptureVerseEnd":36},{"verse":37,"text":"He spake also a parable - Taken from clothes and wine; therefore peculiarly proper at a feast.","sourceParagraph":17,"scriptureVerseStart":36,"scriptureVerseEnd":36},{"verse":38,"text":"39.","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":39,"scriptureVerseEnd":39},{"verse":39,"text":"And no man having drunk old wine - And beside, men are not wont to be immediately freed from old prejudices.","sourceParagraph":18,"scriptureVerseStart":39,"scriptureVerseEnd":39}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Luke","chapter":5}}